{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3zQZDsNb3kywwNuqKy8zd","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Machine learning over the certified corpus: instance structure -> optimum.\n\nThe corpus holds 6,376 instances whose optimum is *proved*, which makes it a\nsupervised dataset with no label noise -- an unusual position for a learned\nmodel of an NP-hard problem, where training targets are normally whatever a\nsolver managed within its budget.\n\nWhat is learned here never becomes a bound. A predicted value is not a proof\nand a model that predicted one point too high would make the search start above\nthe optimum and return a wrong answer that still passes witness verification --\nthe failure mode `satisfiability.mosp_solver._lower_bound` is careful about.\nPredictions are used for analysis, for ordering work, and for choosing between\nsolvers; orderings a model proposes are checked by simulation like any other.\n\"\"\"\n369:def check_timeout_for(solve_seconds: float, floor: float = 30.0, factor: float = 3.0) -> float:\n370-    \"\"\"The checker's wall budget: backward checking is usually cheaper than\n371-    solving but not by a guaranteed factor; measured 0.3-3x on this corpus.\"\"\"\n372-    return max(floor, factor * solve_seconds)\n373-\n374-\n375-def refute_with_proof(\n341:def check_certificate(cert: ProofCertificate, proof_dir: Path = PROOF_DIR,\n342-                      checker: Path = DRAT_TRIM, timeout: float | None = None,\n343-                      keep_cnf: bool = False) -> ProofCertificate:\n344-    \"\"\"Run drat-trim on a stored proof; record verdict and seconds in the certificate.\n345-\n346-    The CNF written by `solve_with_proof` is removed afterwards unless\n347-    `keep_cnf`: it regenerates from the certificate (`rebuild_cnf`).\n348-    \"\"\"\n349-    if cert.status != \"unsat\":\n350-        return cert\n351-    cert.checker = str(checker)\n352-    cnf_gz = proof_dir / f\"{cert.proof_stem}.cnf.gz\"\n353- 