sts/test_obstruction_expansion.py` (24, of which 6 are this item's).*","+","+### 3.1 What was done","+","+**The question.** Item 02 left family E bracketed on 148 of the 436 targets","+in `gap338 ∪ cs200` (145 of the 338, 3 more Chu & Stuckey): the ceiling","+(the search's `max_t (f̂(t) − t) + 1`) above the floor (Harper's bound with","+`f` proved by branch and bound to cap 12). Above cap 12 the branch and bound","+does not finish, so this item asks the inner minimum of a SAT solver: for a","+level `t` and a target `b`, \"is there a set `C` of at least `t` customers","+with `|N[C]| ≤ b`?\" UNSAT proves `f(t) ≥ b + 1`, hence `pw ≥ b + 1 − t` and","+`MOSP ≥ b + 2 − t` by the contrapositive of `exists_closedNbhd_card_le`","+(`lean/MOSPFormalization/EmptyPair.lean`) and `mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`;","+SAT returns a set that lowers `f̂(t)`, so the ceiling drops. Either answer","+moves one half of the bracket, and the level is settled when the two meet.","+","+**The encoding** (`learning/obstruction_expansion.py::expansion_cnf`, the","+contract `ENCODING_SPEC`, plan §0.5 (d)): `x_v` (`v ∈ C`), `y_v`","+(`v ∈ N[C]`), the clauses `x_u → y_v` for every `v ∈ N[u]` including `u`, a","+full totalizer over the `x` with the unit `o_t` (`Σ x ≥ t`) and one over the","+`y` with the unit `¬o_{b+1}` (`Σ y ≤ b`), the auxiliaries of the two","+totalizers in disjoint ranges allocated in a fixed order (the","+`mosp_encoding.py` discipline). The totalizer is ours, not pysat's","+`CardEnc`: the contract has to fix every variable number so that the","+checker can regenerate the clause set, and a library's allocation order is","+not a contract. The clause set is canonical (sorted literals, sorted","+distinct clauses) and the certificate carries the SHA-256 of its DIMACS","+text. `exact_sat(closed, t, b, proof_dir)` solves it with CaDiCaL 1.9.5","+through pysat with proof logging, under a conflict budget (2 × 10⁶) and a","+wall deadline (120 s) — pysat's CaDiCaL cannot be interrupted, so with a","+deadline the call runs in a forked child that is killed at the deadline","+and dies with its parent (`PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`); the proof is read after a","+C-side flush, as `learning/proofs.py` learnt to; every UNSAT is checked by","+`drat-trim` at once and the certificate JSON (`(t, b)`, the CNF's hash","+and size, the gzipped proof and its hash, the solver, the conflicts, the","+checker's binary hash and verdict) is written beside it. A SAT model's set","+is re-evaluated from the masks and never read from the `y` variables; a","+model with more than `t` members is cut to `t` (a subset's closed","+neighbourhood is smaller).","+","+**The driver** (`--stage sat`): for each instance of `gap338` then `cs200`,","+smallest `n` first, the levels the ceiling marks relevant — `t` above the","+proved cap with `f̂(t) − t + 1 > floor` (the item's `≥ floor − 1` in","+pathwidth units includes equality; a level at the floor can neither raise","+it nor move the bracket, so equality is left out), nearest the argmax `t*`","+first, at most 8 per instance — and at each level a descent in `b` from","+`f̂(t) − 1`: the first probe asks whether the incumbent is the minimum","+(UNSAT settles the level in one call, which is the common case: item 02's","+search attains `f` at 99.2% of levels at `n ≤ 22`); after a SAT answer","+(a new incumbent, `f̂(t)` falls) or a censored call the next probe is the","+midpoint of what is unresolved, so a censored boundary still leaves the","+cheaper, lower `b` to try; an UNSAT at any `b` raises the floor to","+`b + 2 − t` even when the level is not settled (\"partial\"). 240 s per","+instance, a hard stop at 6 core-hours (wall × workers), 8 workers at","+`nice 19`, the machine's load 2–6 during the run. The exact floor after the","+run is the cap-12 floor raised by every SAT-proved level; the ceiling after","+the run is `max_t (f̂(t) − t) + 1` over the incumbents with the proved levels","+exact. Outputs: `levels.csv` (one row per call), `instances.csv` (one row","+per instance), `certificates/<instance>/` (`instance.mosp` in the standard","+format, `calls.jsonl`, `summary.json`, and per proved level","+`t<t>_b<b>.json` with `t<t>_b<b>.drat.gz`), `boundary.csv`, `tables.md`.","+","+**The checker** (`paper1/obstruction_check.py check-expansion <instance.mosp>","+<certificate.json>`): its own reader of the standard format, its own MOSP","+graph (a clique per pattern), its own totalizer from the contract, which it","+carries verbatim in its docstring (the test pins the two texts equal; the","+checker imports nothing from `learning/`, `satisfiability/`,","+`pathwidth_solver/` or `mosp/`), regenerates the CNF, compares its hash and","+size with the certificate's, compares the SHA-256 of the instance's rows,","+decompresses the proof, runs `drat-trim` on the regenerated CNF and prints","+the bound with the theorems it rests on; exit status 0 only when every","+check passes. The instance file the checker reads is the one the run wrote","+beside the certificate; the certificate records the benchmark file it came","+from (`source_file`), and the rows' hash ties the two.","+","+### 3.2 Numbers","+","+**The headline.** Of the 148 targets with a bracket after item 02 (145 of","+the 338, 3 more in `cs200`), 144 were reached within the budget and the","+bracket closed on **72**: the family's duality gap is now exact on 264 of","+the 338 (193 after item 02), the floor rose on 85 targets and the ceiling","+fell on 3. **Where it closes is a question of size, not of level**: every","+bracket at 30–60 customers closed (1 + 19 + 48 of 68, all argmax levels","+settled, every one in a single UNSAT call at the incumbent or after one SAT","+answer), 2 of 13 at 75, 1 of 41 at 76–100 (a SCOOP instance), 0 of 22 at","+101–134. The run used **5.76 core-hours** of instance time and stopped at","+its 6-core-hour cap with 3 instances not reached (`Random-125-125-8-5_0` of","+the 338; `Random-100-50-2-2_0` and `Random-100-50-2-4_0` of `cs200` only).","+","+| target | had bracket | reached | bracket closed | argmax settled | floor raised | ceiling lowered | floor gap before → after | bracket before → after | closed by floor | ruled out by ceiling | open with bracket | floor > reference |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| `gap338` | 145 | 143 | 71 | 70 | 84 | 3 | 3.79 → 3.41 | 2.13 → 1.74 | 7 → **12** | 320 | 11 → **6** | 87 → **98** |","+| `cs200` | 84 | 81 | 15 | 15 | 27 | 0 | 3.90 → 3.68 | 3.00 → 2.79 | 57 → 58 | 136 | 7 → 6 | 70 → 74 |","+","+(`tables.md` (a); \"reference\" is the harness's `max(lb_best, tw + 1)`.)","+The five instances the exact floor newly closes on the 338 are `p2540n3_0`","+(8 → 10 = optimum), `Random-50-50-2-1_0` (13 → 15), `p4050n10_0` (11 → 14),","+`p4050n4_0` and `p4050n7_0` (12 → 14); on all five the cap-12 branch and","+bound had the right argmax level in sight and the SAT call proved its","+incumbent in under 6 s. The six of the 338 still open with a bracket are","+all dense and large — `Random-100-100-4-2_0` (floor 40, ceiling = optimum","+50), `100-100-6-3_0` (55 / 61), `100-50-10-1_0` (64 / 68), `125-125-8-1_0`","+(94 / 95), `8-3_0` (92 / 95), `8-4_0` (93 / 94) — the instances where Harper","+*could* be tight and the inner minimum at `t ≈ 15–25` on a 100–125-vertex","+graph is what no call finishes (below).","+","+**The floor, by band of the 338** (`tables.md` (b); mean gap `optimum −","+floor`, optimum units): 9–20: 2.06 → 2.06 (no bracket to close; the family","+is ruled out by its ceiling on all 17); 21–30: 1.98 → 1.98; 31–40: 1.96 →","+**1.49**; 41–60: 2.78 → **1.43**; 61–75: 4.88 → 3.65; 76–100: 8.51 → 8.29;","+101–134: 11.00 → 10.84. Where the floor rose, it rose by 1.15 at 31–40","+(max 2), 1.52 at 41–60 (max 3), 2.33 at 61–75 (max 4), 1.67 at 76–100 and","+2.0 at 101–134 (max 3): the SAT half adds one to four stacks to the cap-12","+floor, and at 41–60 it removes half of the family's remaining gap. Thirteen","+instances had their floor raised by a *partial* level alone (an UNSAT at a","+`b` below the incumbent, the level itself unsettled) — the midpoint probe","+after a censored call is what bought these.","+","+**The ceiling fell on three instances**, all by one and all through the SAT","+answers' sets: `Warwick 1299` (11 → 10 = floor: duality gap exactly 2","+against an optimum of 12), `p2550n8_0` (9 → 8 = floor; optimum 11) and","+**`scoop-A_FA+AA-_6_0`** (79 customers; 8 → 7 = floor; optimum **13**),","+where nine SAT answers at `t = 30–52` each found a `t`-set one below the","+search's incumbent (the sets' values are in `levels.csv`, column `nbhd`),","+so the family's exact value on that SCOOP instance is **7, six stacks","+below the optimum**, settled on both sides: the exact duality gap of the","+expansion family on an industrial instance. Item 02's second pass had","+already moved the ceiling by ±1 on 1% of the instances at 30–100; the 18","+SAT answers (3 at `n ≤ 40`, 3 at 50, 9 on the 79-vertex SCOOP instance,","+2 at 105, 1 at 134) are the exact-half view of the same ±1 artefact: on","+sparse SCOOP graphs the tabu search's incumbents are off by one at several","+levels at once.","+","+**The boundary in `(n, t)`** (`tables.md` (d), (e); `boundary.csv`). Of 344","+calls, 155 UNSAT (every one verified by drat-trim), 18 SAT, 79 out of","+conflicts (2 × 10⁶), 92 killed at the 120 s deadline, 0 errors. Finished","+share by band of `n` and `t`:","+","+| `n` | `t` 13–15 | 16–20 | 21–25 | 26–30 | 31–40 | 41+ | median s (finished) |","+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|","+| ≤ 60 | 36/36 | 49/49 | — | — | — | — | 0.1–0.8 |","+| 61–75 | 2/2 | 8/17 | 11/19 | 5/10 | 2/4 | — | 15 |","+| 76–100 | 2/6 | 2/23 | 6/31 | 9/19 | 8/28 | 23/29 | 0.8–48 |","+| 101–134 | 0/8 | 0/12 | 0/15 | 0/3 | 3/18 | 7/15 | 15–44 |","+","+Every call at `n ≤ 50` finished (max `t` settled 20 at `n = 50`, in 0.58 s","+at the median, 281 k conflicts at most); at `n = 75` the finished share is","+28 of 52 and the deepest settled level is 15 (`Random-75-75-6-4_0`), the","+shallowest censored 19; at `n = 100` 22 of 108 finished and no level at","+all settled on the `Random` instances (max `t` settled: none), while the","+two SCOOP instances at 79 and 105 settled levels at `t = 52` and `t = 46`","+(28 of 28 and 4 of 5 calls finished: their graphs are sparse, `optimum / n","+≈ 0.1–0.16`, and the CNF a third the size); at `n = 125` 3 of 62 finished,","+all at `t ≥ 33` and `b ≤ 49`, levels the ceiling marks but far from the","+argmax. **The boundary is `n ≈ 60–75` on the Chu & Stuckey graphs at the","+levels that matter (`t* ≈ 0.2–0.35 n`), and it is a boundary in `n` at a","+given density rather than in `t`**: the finished share at 76–100 *rises*","+with `t` (0.09 at 16–20 to 0.79 at 41+) because the deep levels are the","+sparse instances' and `b` is close to `n` there (the `Σ y ≤ b` totalizer is","+nearly free), while at 101–134 nothing below `t = 31` finishes. Clause","+counts are 4–6 k at `n ≤ 50`, 14 k at 75, 24–26 k at 100 and 36–41 k at 125;","+the finished calls' conflicts reach 1.3 M at 75 and 1.1 M at 100, so the","+2 × 10⁶ budget is binding at the boundary rather than generous: a 10× budget","+would move it by one band at most, on the exponential the `t`-profile","+shows, and is not what the plan's §0.8 (1) risk asked (the risk is","+realised as stated). The analogue of §17's `m² · k ≈ 10⁴` is **`n ≈ 75` at","+`optimum / n ≈ 0.2–0.5`**, i.e. the dense half of the Chu & Stuckey corpus","+above 60 customers is out of the exact half's reach at 2 × 10⁶ conflicts","+and 120 s per call; drat-trim's check costs 0.3–3× the solve (median 15–45 s","+at 75–125, 1,127 s in total for the 158 certificates on disk, the largest","+proof 38.7 MB gzipped, every one under the 50 MB limit and kept).","+","+**The certificates.** 158 certificate files on disk (155 from the 144","+reached instances, with their rows in `levels.csv`; 3 on the two `cs200`","+instances the cap interrupted, valid but outside the tables — they prove","+`f(43) ≥ 46` on `Random-100-50-2-2_0` and `f(45) ≥ 48` on `-2-4_0`, both","+below those instances' floors), **158 of 158 verified** by","+`paper1/obstruction_check.py` (`checker_verdicts.csv`): the regenerated CNF's","+hash and size equal the certificate's on every one, the rows' hash ties the","+instance, drat-trim verifies the proof on the regenerated CNF, max 45 s.","+Every bound the item claims is read off a certificate in that file and","+rests on `exists_closedNbhd_card_le` (contrapositive) and","+`mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`, both `sorry`-free in the development; the","+checker trusts drat-trim and those two theorems and nothing of ours.","+","+### 3.3 Through the harness","+","+`run_harness.py --workers 8`: the exact floor as a lookup candidate","+(`sat_floor`: the run's `floor_after` by the SHA-256 of the instance's rows,","+1 where the run has no record) through `learning.bound_harness`'s validity","+stage on all 6,376 corpus instances (`harness_table.md`): **above optimum","+0**; beats the reference `max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on **74 of the 338** (item","+02's cap-12 floor at 10 s: 73; at item 01's 60 s and item 02's 600 s, the","+cap-12 floor already stood above the reference on 87 of the 338, and the","+exact floor on 98, `tables.md` (a) — the harness's 74 counts the 144","+instances the run reached and nothing else). The ledger's guard (item 01)","+and the run's own guard (`floor_after ≤ optimum`, `floor_after ≤","+ceiling_after`, asserted in `tests/test_obstruction_expansion.py::test_committed_sat_files`)","+hold on every row.","+","+### 3.4 Kill verdict and compute","+","+**Kill criterion (plan §0.9, E-exact): met, narrowly on the sensible","+reading and clearly on the literal one.** SAT settled the argmax level on","+70 of the 145 instances of the 338 that had a bracket (48.3%, against the","+criterion's 50%); counted over the 338, the argmax level is settled on 264","+(78.1%) after the run, 70 of them by SAT (20.7%). The record therefore","+says: **Harper exact is out of reach by SAT above cap 12 at 75 customers and","+beyond on the Chu & Stuckey graphs** (boundary `n ≈ 60–75` at the argmax","+levels, 2 × 10⁶ conflicts, 120 s per call) **and fully in reach to 60**,","+where every bracket closed in seconds. The family's floor downstream is the","+exact floor where a verified certificate proves it (144 instances,","+`instances.csv::floor_after`) and the cap-12 floor elsewhere; nothing in","+the floor rests on the search's quality or on a censored level. The second","+kill condition — an UNSAT at a `(t, b)` where item 02's enumeration has a","+set — occurred on **0** calls (the self-test at `n ≤ 12` agrees with the","+enumeration on 3,000+ `(t, b)` pairs over 100 graphs, and the run's SAT","+answers all have `|N[set]| ≤ b` re-evaluated from the masks).","+","+**Compute.** Instance time 5.76 core-hours (solve 5.24, in-run drat-trim","+0.45, the rest the forks and the writes), the checker sweep 0.31, the","+harness run under 0.01 (a lookup), the smoke run and four timing probes","+≈ 0.1: **≈ 6.2 core-hours** against the item's 6; the overrun is the","+independent re-check the acceptance criteria require. 8 workers at","+`nice 19`; the machine's one-minute load was 2–8 during the run (the","+owner's `run_unlimited.py` was not running). Wall 45 min.","+","+### 3.5 What this does not claim","+","+That the SAT route scales beyond the boundary it measures (a call censored","+by its conflict budget or its deadline says nothing about `f(t)`, and no","+censored call contributes to any floor); that a larger budget would not","+move the boundary (not measured; the conflict counts of the finished calls","+at 75–100 say a 10× budget would at most reach one more band); that the","+exact floor on the 144 reached instances is the family's best (levels the","+ceiling did not mark, and the three unreached instances, were not asked;","+at most 8 levels per instance and 240 s, which at `n ≥ 75` meant one or","+two levels); that the ceiling after the run is the family's value (it is an","+upper estimate still, exact only where it meets the floor: 72 targets); any","+solver change (no candidate reaches `_lower_bound`; the family's bound as a","+bound inside the search was a net loss, `reports/expansion_bound.md`, which","+this item does not revisit). The certificate for an instance is a proof","+about *that instance file*: the checker reads the `.mosp` file the run","+wrote beside it and ties it to the benchmark source by the rows' hash","+recorded in the certificate, not by re-reading the benchmark file's own","+format. \"We found no prior report\" of DRAT-certified vertex-isoperimetric","+profiles on MOSP instances; the bound is Harper (1966), the totalizer","+Bailleux & Boufkhad (2003), the checker drat-trim (Wetzler, Heule & Hunt","+2014)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D6E9XA4y3vyjVDjjLkKLZE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
